From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander A <st7105@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 01 Nov 2026 08:48:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: detect the bind sockaddr API in target headers

Stable kernels can backport the sockaddr_unsized bind callback without
changing their major/minor version. Detect the API in the target kernel's
net.h instead of relying on a version threshold.

Use srctree during Kbuild so cross-compilation does not inspect host
headers. Use ccflags-y so a command-line EXTRA_CFLAGS does not discard
the feature define. Keep the original callback on older kernels.

Related upstream change:
https://github.com/ntop/PF_RING/commit/94a7d317ad91dd8c0671d2278fc3ebe58fbe6326

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Alexander A <st7105@gmail.com>
---
--- a/kernel/Makefile
+++ b/kernel/Makefile
@@ -4,6 +4,13 @@
 
 obj-m := pf_ring.o
 
+# Detect the callback API in the target kernel, including stable backports.
+ifneq ($(KERNELRELEASE),)
+ifneq ($(shell grep -w sockaddr_unsized $(srctree)/include/linux/net.h),)
+ccflags-y += -DHAVE_SOCKADDR_UNSIZED
+endif
+endif
+
 # assigned by Makefile.dkms
 GIT_REV:=
 
--- a/kernel/pf_ring.c
+++ b/kernel/pf_ring.c
@@ -5861,7 +5861,11 @@ static int packet_ring_bind(struct sock
 /* ************************************* */
 
 /* Bind to a device */
+#ifdef HAVE_SOCKADDR_UNSIZED
+static int ring_bind(struct socket *sock, struct sockaddr_unsized *sa, int addr_len)
+#else
 static int ring_bind(struct socket *sock, struct sockaddr *sa, int addr_len)
+#endif
 {
   struct sock *sk = sock->sk;
   struct net *net = sock_net(sk);
